{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "042Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nU \\longmapsto \\Ob(\\mathcal{S}_U)/\\!\\!\\cong\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-setoid-fibres}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stack-in-setoids-characterize}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:da9ea2b514dbfd7e63a100a1da5e7c271a164c6c75046abdb2c718bdd2be0a3e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:15f0ec2a9802360b1bd5f8ddf6cd47984225499538d0dff8ccf463f1e9d2a5b0", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a category fibred in setoids over <MATH_0003>.\nThen <MATH_0004> is a stack in setoids if and only if the unique\nequivalent category <MATH_0005> fibred in sets (see\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>)\nis a stack in sets. In other words, if and only if the presheaf\n<MATH_0006>\nis a sheaf.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1d96f4deb6b56aa11197b60123aeb00b5264c4385aa5fc115291a9204c8b554e", "unit_id": "tag:0432:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "042Y", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7b255fc76bb0bbe9c4def579cbae2f7d7790541c026b4afecc55a9702cd2e61b", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:0432:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "042Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stack-in-setoids-equivalent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7a06d8cecc2e4ffe3e65ef19e939456917e6e4d2d4b8b74b82b626d9d5802132", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9e7c978913f076e040158fdea03fb3ebb55d9a50731a806d5e7adeadc5dcb939", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> be categories over <MATH_0004>.\nSuppose that <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are equivalent\nas categories over <MATH_0007>.\nThen <MATH_0008> is a stack in setoids over <MATH_0009> if and only if\n<MATH_0010> is a stack in setoids over <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b17ae1f96599a15b2cc2471003a36c30fcfc42408203398c8b055d7f250f6eef", "unit_id": "tag:0431:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "042Y", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-setoid-fibres}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-stack-in-setoids-characterize}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:16cb629c15cecc1cf0cb6a206a9697fcf1f78aef4800212e12a9836749ac8ed5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:70ceb3d417db2a7de05d417cb6ebd616116ad6e76951e180437ac1b62bea5875", "source_text": "By\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe see that a category <MATH_0001> over <MATH_0002> is fibred in setoids\nover <MATH_0003> if and only if it is equivalent over <MATH_0004>\nto a category fibred in sets.\nHence we see that <MATH_0005> is fibred in setoids over <MATH_0006>\nif and only if <MATH_0007> is fibred in setoids over <MATH_0008>.\nHence now the lemma follows from\nLemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:af8bb18ff268e82c2911a8185f0044a2b742d60e2b2f09db3be49f3d082dc1df", "unit_id": "tag:0431:proof"}
